Where to look





What owns an item?



items.list_id → lists, items.team_id → teams, items.owner_id → user_profiles





How do goals attach to teams?



goals.team_id, goal_team_associations





How do items move teams/lists?



item_movements (+ pending fields on items)





KB tree?



knowledge_base → article_hierarchy_nodes.parent_id (self) → articles / documents





Meeting content?



meetings ↔ headlines_meetings / cascading_messages_meetings / meeting_segments





Who can do what?



permission_catalog + user_permission_grants / role_default_permissions





Suggested live-DEV reconciliation SQL

-- Public tables on this environment
SELECT table_name
FROM information_schema.tables
WHERE table_schema = 'public'
  AND table_type = 'BASE TABLE'
ORDER BY 1;

-- FK edges on this environment
SELECT
  tc.table_name AS from_table,
  kcu.column_name AS from_column,
  ccu.table_name AS to_table,
  ccu.column_name AS to_column
FROM information_schema.table_constraints tc
JOIN information_schema.key_column_usage kcu
  ON tc.constraint_name = kcu.constraint_name
 AND tc.table_schema = kcu.table_schema
JOIN information_schema.constraint_column_usage ccu
  ON ccu.constraint_name = tc.constraint_name
 AND ccu.table_schema = tc.table_schema
WHERE tc.constraint_type = 'FOREIGN KEY'
  AND tc.table_schema = 'public'
ORDER BY 1, 2;

Compare that result set to the edge list above to spot DEV vs repo drift.





